Title: Use base::wstring instead of std::wstring
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: The ABIv11 libstdc++ is built without wchar_t support and has no std::wstring alias; base, she and ui use std::wstring and do not compile. base/thread.cpp yield() fell back to select(), which the ABIv11 SDK does not declare. base/string.cpp compared wchar_t with int (-Wsign-compare where wchar_t is unsigned).
Change: base/string.h: typedef std::basic_string<wchar_t> base::wstring, used instead of std::wstring everywhere outside Windows-only files. this_thread::yield() calls sched_yield() on AROS. insert_utf8_char compares as unsigned long.
Scope: all platforms (no behaviour change)
Upstream: candidate
Verification: ABIv11 (AROS One, pool v11-3, 2026-11-16): builds with no warnings with GCC 10.5 and SDK-202609; started from a Shell with a 262144-byte stack, new sprite, drawing, PNG save with Enter, Intuition menu, AROS Capture picture pasted, LibreSprite picture shown by MultiView CLIPBOARD, clean exit (no task or pthread left). Mainline x86_64 rebuilt with no warnings.
Removal: when upstream adopts it.
---
